Water","amount":"200ml","buy":null,"q":200.0,"u":"ml","img":"/data/food/photos/ingredients/5748517b4dab717e338b4567.png"},{"name":"Honey","amount":"1 tbsp","buy":"Honey","q":1.0,"u":"tbsp","img":"/data/food/photos/ingredients/6172cb313021d49a7feafc84.png"},{"name":"Butter","amount":"20g","buy":"Butter","q":20.0,"u":"g","img":"/data/food/photos/ingredients/60c73507053f5e815cd52d5b.png"}],"steps":[{"points":["Boil a half-full kettle.","Drain the sweetcorn. Peel and grate the garlic (or use a garlic press).","Heat a frying pan on medium-high heat (no oil).","Once hot, fry the pork and roasted spice and herb blend, 5-6 mins. Break up the mince as it cooks."],"notes":[{"kind":"important","text":"Wash hands and utensils after handling raw meat. Cook so there's no pink in the middle."}],"image":"/data/food/photos/steps/676959f10200888b9f0f454a-1.jpg","title":"Get Frying"},{"points":["Put the couscous into a bowl.","Pour in the boiling water (see pantry). Stir in half the chicken stock paste.","Cover tightly with cling film. Leave to the side, 10 mins.","Drain the fat from the mince. Season with salt and pepper."],"notes":[],"image":"/data/food/photos/steps/676959f10200888b9f0f454a-2.jpg","title":"Cook Couscous"},{"points":["Add the garlic to the pork and cook, 1 min more.","Stir in the sweetcorn, passata, chipotle (add less if you'd prefer things milder), honey, butter (see pantry for both) and remaining chicken stock paste.","Bring to the boil and simmer, 2-3 mins.","Add the spinach in handfuls, making sure it's piping hot, 1-2 mins. Add a splash of water if it's a little thick."],"notes":[],"image":"/data/food/photos/steps/676959f10200888b9f0f454a-3.jpg","title":"Flavour Town"},{"points":["Fluff the couscous up with a fork. Share between your bowls.","Spoon over the chipotle pork.","Top with the smashed avocado. Dollop on the soured cream."],"notes":[],"image":"/data/food/photos/steps/676959f10200888b9f0f454a-4.jpg","title":"Dinner's Ready!"}]}